Impeccable is a design skill for web and native interfaces (version 4.6.0 was the source). raea rewrote it for
timed short-form video with sound, made by raea's video agent (void) from real footage. Every adapted file says so
in its first line. The changes, in general: web surfaces became timed pieces on a phone; viewports became frames
and the first 1.5 seconds; DOM/CSS detectors became perception and render lints; contrast, measure and type limits
became cap heights, reading time and platform UI zones; the comp-led image path, live mode, the decision page and
all scripts were dropped (raea generates no imagery; the agent's "comp" is a rendered frame of real footage).

